<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Subtlety Rogues</span></span></h2>Crafted items are a great way to get an early boost to your item level and bolster up your stats. While some do require you to be leveled up in the profession that crafts them, there are several BoE options as well that can be bought and sold.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77534/agile-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Agile Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile Retinal Armor</span></a>, as with every other expansion, has <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> offering the best helm option we have prior to raiding. It can be socket with Tinker's Gears, such as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77542/quick-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Quick Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Tinker's Gear</span></a>, allowing you to pick and choose which secondaries you will benefit from.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85824/greyshadow-gloves">
<img alt="Greyshadow Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_leather_raidrogue_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greyshadow Gloves</span></a> is our Pre-BiS glove option, a crafted BoE from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> profession.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85823/greyshadow-chestguard">
<img alt="Greyshadow Chestguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greyshadow Chestguard</span></a> is our Pre-BiS chest option, a crafted BoE from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> profession.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85828/murderers-gloves">
<img alt="Murderer's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Murderer's Gloves</span></a> is an excellent glove option that becomes available after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6125/mogushan-vaults">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mogu'shan Vaults</span></a> raid, where the pattern drops.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85788/chestguard-of-nemeses">
<img alt="Chestguard of Nemeses" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raidrogue_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestguard of Nemeses</span></a> is an excellent chest option that becomes available after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6125/mogushan-vaults">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mogu'shan Vaults</span></a> raid, where the pattern drops.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82974/masterwork-ghost-shard">
<img alt="Masterwork Ghost Shard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_knife_1h_pandariatradeskill_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Masterwork Ghost Shard</span></a> is a great <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=164/blacksmithing">
<img alt="Blacksmithing" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_blacksmithing.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blacksmithing</span></a> crafted BoE weapon that will serve as a great placeholder until you can get a better itemized 463 option.</div></li></ul>Phase 3 offers us a couple of new powerful 522 iLvl pieces that <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> can craft!<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94269/quilen-hide-boots">
<img alt="Quilen Hide Boots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_leather_raidrogue_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quilen Hide Boots</span></a> is an excellent feet option that becomes available after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> raid, where the pattern drops.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94270/quilen-hide-helm">
<img alt="Quilen Hide Helm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_leather_raidrogue_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quilen Hide Helm</span></a> is an excellent helm option that becomes available after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> raid, where the pattern drops.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Pre-Raid Subtlety Rogue Trinkets</span></span></h2>While our absolute BiS trinkets are very easy to figure out and are set in stone, it may be hard to acquire both of these or you may not have the profession needed to acquire them. For this reason, we'll list both the best trinkets and a couple of alternatives that you can aim for while waiting for drops to happen.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>The best trinkets are generally the ones that best align with your big DPS cooldowns.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89082/hawkmasters-talon">
<img alt="Hawkmaster's Talon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_monsterhorn_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hawkmaster's Talon</span></a> offers a high amount of static Agility, with a massive Haste proc that can be lined up with our cooldowns.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86043/jade-bandit-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Bandit Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_honoramongstthieves.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Bandit Figurine</span></a> is a BoE trinket that drops in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6125/mogushan-vaults">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mogu'shan Vaults</span></a> raid. It has the exact same stats as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89082/hawkmasters-talon">
<img alt="Hawkmaster's Talon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_monsterhorn_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hawkmaster's Talon</span></a> and is a decent consideration if you have excess gold and want to use your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> for other pieces.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is an amazing trinket that offers both static Agility and an Agility proc. This trinket is far and away the best pre-raid option and will last you all the way until you get both Heroic raid options. You can get this trinket by obtaining the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79323/tiger-deck">
<img alt="Tiger Deck" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_deck_whitetiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tiger Deck</span></a>, crafted from the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=773/inscription">
<img alt="Inscription" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tradeskill01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription</span></a> profession.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is a great Pre-BiS trinket option, giving a high amount of Mastery as well as having a strong Agility proc to play around. This item comes from being leveled up in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86890/terror-in-the-mists">
<img alt="Terror in the Mists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Terror in the Mists</span></a> is another good trinket option, with static Agility and a Critical Strike proc. This ends up being a great Pre-BiS option if you don't have the gold for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> or the profession for <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86791/bottle-of-infinite-stars">
<img alt="Bottle of Infinite Stars" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottle of Infinite Stars</span></a> is essentially a worse version of <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Phase 3 Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="last">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94511/vicious-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Vicious Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_speedoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vicious Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is technically able to be acquired outside of raid; however, it'll require a bit of grinding. Though if acquired, it greatly outperforms the competition.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95625/renatakis-soul-charm">
<img alt="Renataki's Soul Charm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Renataki's Soul Charm</span></a> is our other trinket option that provides a generous amount of Agility over 10 seconds.<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95665/bad-juju">
<img alt="Bad Juju" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_troll_voodoodoll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bad Juju</span></a> gives you a large burst of Agility with a silly proc of summoning 3 voodoo gnomes! The Mastery it offers can be reforged to give us a solid chunk of Haste as well.</div></li>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Subtlety Rogues</span></span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as racial weapon expertise, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer miss dungeon or raid bosses. Our Poisons are now also based off the melee hit table, meaning that 7.5% is all that it takes to ensure that our Poisons never miss. Your regular swings (white damage) still have a chance to miss until the dual-wield Hit cap of 26.5%. This is calculated by taking the base miss chance of 3%, adding the dual-wield penalty of 19%, then adding 1.5% per level above you the enemy is, for a total cap of 26.5%.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them when attacked from the front. For the vast majority of bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry attacks from behind.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Gemming for Subtlety Rogues</span></span></h2>Gemming is fairly straightforward throughout Mists of Pandaria. You look to get as much Agility as possible and tend to make socket bonus choices based if they will give you more Agility or equal Agility with additional secondary stats. The new <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> arrives in Phase 3. It'll require you to kill bosses in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> and acquire 20 <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94593/secrets-of-the-empire">
<img alt="Secrets of the Empire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/secrets_of_the_empire_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Secrets of the Empire</span></a>, as well as 40 <a class="q2 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=72095/trillium-bar">
<img alt="Trillium Bar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ingot_trillium.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trillium Bar</span></a>. This new gem brings the buff <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=137596/capacitance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_purge.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitance</span></a>. The PPM for different specializations varies quite a bit.<br/>
<br/>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
